                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "x^6-6x^4+15x^2-20+\\frac{15}{x^2}-\\frac{6}{x^4}+\\frac{1}{x^6}",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p4-q36-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Use row 6 coefficients with alternating signs, then simplify powers.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Use row 6 coefficients $1,6,15,20,15,6,1$, treating the second term as $-x$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\left(\\frac1x-x\\right)^6&=\\left(\\frac1x\\right)^6+6\\left(\\frac1x\\right)^5(-x)+15\\left(\\frac1x\\right)^4(-x)^2+20\\left(\\frac1x\\right)^3(-x)^3\\\\&\\quad +15\\left(\\frac1x\\right)^2(-x)^4+6\\left(\\frac1x\\right)(-x)^5+(-x)^6\\\\\\left(\\frac1x-x\\right)^6&=\\frac1{x^6}-\\frac6{x^4}+\\frac{15}{x^2}-20+15x^2-6x^4+x^6\\\\\\left(\\frac1x-x\\right)^6&=x^6-6x^4+15x^2-20+\\frac{15}{x^2}-\\frac6{x^4}+\\frac1{x^6}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      },
